{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"6fc67571","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.004572,"end_time":"2026-10-23T05:54:24.88645+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T05:54:24.881878+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# 🧠 Gemma 3 AI News Summarizer — Kaggle Training Notebook\n","\n","**Model**: `google/gemma-3-4b-it` or `google/gemma-3-12b-it` (text-only, via `kagglehub`)\n","**Method**: QLoRA (4-bit NF4 quantisation + LoRA adapters)\n","**Library**: TRL `SFTTrainer` + PEFT\n","**Hardware**: Kaggle T4 × 2 (16 GB VRAM each = 32 GB total)\n","**Est. Time**: ~45 min (4B) · ~90 min (12B) for 1 epoch on 3 500 examples\n","\n","---\n","\n","## Why Gemma 3 instead of Gemma 4?\n","\n","| | Gemma 4 E4B | Gemma 3 4B | Gemma 3 12B |\n","|---|---|---|---|\n","| Architecture | Multimodal | Text-only ✅ | Text-only ✅ |\n","| T4 VRAM (4-bit) | ~9 GB | ~5 GB ✅ | ~9 GB ✅ |\n","| `AutoTokenizer` | ❌ (needs Processor) | ✅ | ✅ |\n","| BF16 support | Required (T4 ❌) | FP16 fine ✅ | FP16 fine ✅ |\n","| Fine-tune stability | ⚠️ Fragile | ✅ Excellent | ✅ Excellent |\n","\n","Gemma 4 is a multimodal model. Its vision tower adds memory overhead and\n","the `AutoProcessor` path is fragile on T4 GPUs. For **text summarization**,\n","Gemma 3 is faster, lighter, and fully supported by TRL out of the box.\n","\n","---\n","\n","## ✅ Prerequisites (do these BEFORE running)\n","\n","1. Go to https://www.kaggle.com/models/google/gemma-3\n","2. Click **\"Request Access\"** → **\"Verify via Kaggle Account\"** → Submit\n","3. Attach the model: Add-ons → Models → search **\"gemma-3\"** → add `gemma-3-4b-it`\n","4. Enable GPU: Settings → Accelerator → **GPU T4 × 2**\n","5. Attach your dataset: Add-ons → Datasets → **`deetyam/gemma-news-data`**\n","\n","## ♻️ Checkpoint / Resume\n","\n","- Checkpoints are saved every 10 optimiser steps to `/kaggle/working/checkpoints/`.\n","- To resume, set `RESUME_FROM_CHECKPOINT = True` in Section 4 — the latest checkpoint\n","  is found automatically.\n","- To resume from a specific checkpoint, set it to the path string (e.g. `\"/kaggle/working/checkpoints/checkpoint-80\"`)."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"8101d10e","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.003881,"end_time":"2026-10-23T05:54:24.894193+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T05:54:24.890312+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 1. Install Dependencies\n","\n","> Run this cell first, then **restart the kernel** before continuing."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"1622a24f","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-23T05:54:24.903792Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-23T05:54:24.903204Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-23T05:54:32.931993Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-23T05:54:32.931124Z"},"papermill":{"duration":8.035715,"end_time":"2026-10-23T05:54:32.933581+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-23T05:54:24.897866+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["\u001b[2K     \u001b[90m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m \u001b[32m40.4/40.4 kB\u001b[0m \u001b[31m1.1 MB/s\u001b[0m eta \u001b[36m0:00:00\u001b[0m\r\n","\u001b[2K   \u001b[90m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m \u001b[32m927.2/927.2 kB\u001b[0m \u001b[31m5.8 MB/s\u001b[0m eta \u001b[36m0:00:00\u001b[0m\r\n","\u001b[2K   \u001b[90m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m \u001b[32m43.1/43.1 MB\u001b[0m \u001b[31m46.8 MB/s\u001b[0m eta \u001b[36m0:00:00\u001b[0m\r\n","\u001b[2K   \u001b[90m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m \u001b[32m910.1/910.1 kB\u001b[0m \u001b[31m42.8 MB/s\u001b[0m eta \u001b[36m0:00:00\u001b[0m\r\n","\u001b[?25h\n","✅ Installation complete — restart the kernel now, then continue from Section 2.\n"]}],"source":["# ─── Install / upgrade required packages ────────────────────────────────────\n","# Run once, then restart the kernel.\n","!pip install -q \\\n","    \"transformers>=4.46.0\" \\\n","    